& [Purpose]
  + advance Cantor from exact identity and typed-relation navigation toward fast inspectable term association
  + compile admitted semantic text into a deterministic token-posting sidecar whose every association resolves to exact catalogue fabric unit package meaning and source identity
  + keep organized concise expression as a retrieval aid rather than truth authority permission risk or effect authority

& [ActivationDecision]
  + activate Slice4B1 lexical sidecar machine forms tokenizer compiler validator and adversarial fixtures only
  + do not activate lexical query matching ranking candidate contribution budgets cursors result profiles scanner integration direct-query equivalence or corpus measurement
  + preserve scan_exact_semantic_anchors AnchorQuery AnchorBudget AnchorCandidate AssociationContribution AnchorQueryResult and their serialized bytes and behavior unchanged
  + reserve Slice4B2 for a distinct lexical query wrapper budget match-account result-root and scanner activation after Slice4B1 proof

& [Architecture]
  + DerivedLexicalAssociationIndex is a disposable sidecar and never a field inside DerivedSemanticAnchorCatalogue
  + the sidecar binds exact catalogue_root fabric_root tokenizer identity compiler identity index identity index_root and proof_digest
  + exact-only callers neither construct receive nor trust the sidecar
  + sidecar derivation first canonically validates and rebuilds the supplied DerivedSemanticAnchorCatalogue against the same admitted SemanticFabric

& [ClosedForms]
  + LexicalTokenizerIdentity binds profile compiler_id compiler_version and adversarial_fixture_digest
  + LexicalSurfaceKind is PreferredExpression Alias or Meaning
  + LexicalPosting binds normalized token exact SemanticAddress surface kind surface_digest occurrence_count and sorted unique evidence_refs
  + DerivedLexicalAssociationIndex binds profile logical revision exact catalogue and fabric roots tokenizer identity sorted token-to-posting map index_root and proof_digest
  + LexicalIndexDerivationRequest binds index_id logical_revision and tokenizer profile
  + typed lexical derivation faults distinguish invalid request unsupported profile stale roots source correspondence token posting projection and digest failures
  + every form denies unknown fields and every bounded string collection map and count validates before acceptance

& [TokenizerProfile]
  + [profile] cantor-lexical-tokenizer/0.1
  + trim the complete input surface
  + apply the compiled Rust standard library Unicode lowercase mapping
  + split at every character the compiled Rust standard library classifies as non-alphanumeric
  + discard empty runs
  + retain sorted unique tokens for index membership while separately counting repeated occurrences inside one exact surface
  + retain original surface only through its domain-separated digest and admitted source correspondence rather than copying prose into every posting
  + bind compiler version and an exact adversarial fixture digest because Unicode tables and lowercase behavior belong to compiled-toolchain identity
  + perform no Unicode normalization confusable folding stop-word deletion stemming lemmatization synonym expansion edit distance fuzzy matching n-gram generation or learned transform

& [SurfaceAndEvidenceRules]
  + PreferredExpression reads only IdentityAnchorEntry preferred_expression
  + Alias reads each exact sorted IdentityAnchorEntry alias
  + Meaning exact-resolves IdentityAnchorEntry meaning_ref to the corresponding admitted SemanticUnit meaning text and verifies unit and package correspondence
  + surface_digest commits surface kind exact SemanticAddress and original UTF-8 surface bytes under a distinct domain
  + evidence_refs contain only exact admitted identities that establish the address meaning and source correspondence
  + emit one posting per normalized token address surface kind and surface digest
  + occurrence_count is the checked positive number of that token within that exact surface and never contributes authority or ranking in Slice4B1
  + a surface that yields no tokens emits no posting but remains reproducible from admitted source during whole-index rebuild

& [CanonicalDerivation]
  + require the supported request and tokenizer profiles nonempty bounded logical revision and exact compiler constants
  + rebuild and validate the supplied catalogue against the admitted fabric before reading any surface
  + enumerate identity entries addresses surface kinds and surface values in canonical order
  + derive tokens postings and evidence using checked bounded operations
  + sort each posting set by token-external structural identity and reject duplicate posting identities
  + compute index_root from profile revision roots tokenizer identity and canonical postings under a new domain
  + compute proof_digest from request admitted generation compiler identity index_root and exact derivation decisions under a separate domain
  + equal request catalogue fabric compiler and source bytes produce byte-identical sidecars

& [ValidationAndReplay]
  + structural validation refuses empty over-bound or noncanonical tokens postings maps evidence and occurrence counts
  + every posting address exact-resolves in the catalogue and retains the same package unit digest kind context version and source anchors
  + surface kind and digest replay against preferred expression alias or admitted meaning bytes
  + tokenizer replay reproduces token membership and exact occurrence count
  + whole-artifact validation fresh-derives the sidecar from request catalogue and admitted fabric then requires exact equality
  + any supported input mutation changes an owning digest or refuses; no caller-supplied self-consistent sidecar can authorize itself

& [Budgets]
  + compile-time constants bound surface bytes token bytes tokens per surface postings per token total postings evidence references logical revision and serialized sidecar bytes
  + derivation refuses before returning an artifact when any bound is crossed
  + Slice4B1 adds no query-time maximum_lexical_postings field because changing AnchorBudget would violate exact-query byte stability
  + Slice4B2 must define a distinct LexicalAnchorBudget or lexical query wrapper and fail before partial lexical discovery

& [AdversarialAcceptance]
  + preferred expression alias and meaning surfaces derive exact postings with inspectable evidence
  + mixed ASCII case punctuation numeric and one-character tokens are deterministic
  + non-Latin lowercase combining-mark and composed-versus-decomposed inputs follow the declared profile without silent normalization
  + duplicate terms inside one surface increase occurrence_count without duplicating posting identity
  + duplicate tokens across surfaces remain separate surface-identified postings
  + empty-token and over-bound surfaces behave explicitly
  + unknown profile stale catalogue or fabric root wrong compiler fixture surface digest token occurrence evidence ordering posting omission addition and index or proof digest mutations refuse
  + equal derivations serialize byte-identically and a fresh whole-index replay agrees exactly
  + all existing exact catalogue scanner and workspace behavior remains unchanged

& [AuthorityBoundary]
  + the sidecar proposes no candidate performs no gate computes no relevance selects no path and authorizes no instruction or effect
  + token membership is lexical correlation evidence only
  + no provider model attention bridge persistence filesystem database network remote hidden-state shared-forward-pass FPGA OneDrive EVO-X2 or Minecraft behavior
  + direct query exact scanner and iterative-attention paths remain independent rollback surfaces

& [CompletionGate]
  + source manifest SJS review and exact Slice4B1 phase lock precede code
  + focused form compiler validation mutation and replay tests pass
  + full workspace tests warnings-denied Clippy format recursive evidence manifests and diff integrity pass
  + solution proof narrative reentry and Git publication bind exact source dependency implementation and test identities
